.\" sage-secret(1) manpage — mdoc format
.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt SAGE-SECRET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sage-secret
.Nd run a command with secrets from Bitwarden, without writing or showing them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm version
.Nm
.Cm setup
.Fl -server Ar URL
.Nm
.Cm check
.Nm
.Cm run
.Op Fl -env Ar FILE ...
.Fl -
.Ar CMD
.Op Ar ARGS ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs commands with secrets from Bitwarden without writing or showing the
secrets itself. The vault account is an agent account on a self-hosted
Vaultwarden, with one collection of the keys agents need. Its API key and
master password live in the login Keychain under the service
.Sy sage-secret .
.Pp
A reference has the form
.Sy bw:ITEM
or
.Sy bw:ITEM/FIELD .
.Nm
resolves references in environment values and
.Fl -env
files. It passes other file values through unchanged. The four field
forms are
.Sy password
(the default when
.Sy /FIELD
is omitted),
.Sy username ,
.Sy notes ,
and the name of a custom field.
.Pp
Each run that has references logs in if needed, unlocks the vault,
resolves the references, runs the command, and locks the vault again.
The command receives the real secret values.
.Pp
What this protects: secrets never sit in files, in shell history, or in
output
.Nm
prints. What it does not: the command receives the real values, so a
command that prints its environment prints them. A credential-injecting
proxy (level 2) is the step that keeps values away from the command itself.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width 24n
.It Cm version
Print the version,
.Sy 0.1.0 .
.It Cm setup Fl -server Ar URL
Set the Bitwarden CLI server URL. Prompt for the agent account's API key
and master password and store them in the login Keychain without echoing
them.
.It Cm check
Log in if needed, unlock the vault, and print the server, account,
status, and visible item names. It does not print item contents.
.It Cm run Oo Fl -env Ar FILE ... Oc Fl - Ar CMD Op Ar ARGS ...
Read environment values from each
.Fl -env
file, resolving every value that starts with
.Sy bw: .
Values already in the environment are resolved the same way. Run the
command with the resolved values in its environment. The command and its
arguments follow
.Fl - .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width 24n
.It Ev environment variables
.Nm Cm run
checks every value in the inherited environment for a
.Sy bw:
reference and replaces each reference with its resolved secret.
Environment values not beginning with
.Sy bw:
pass through unchanged.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width 36n
.It login Keychain items, service sage-secret
The agent account's credentials are stored as generic-password items
under the service
.Sy sage-secret .
The accounts are
.Sy BW_CLIENTID ,
.Sy BW_CLIENTSECRET ,
and
.Sy BW_PASSWORD .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Configure the vault
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sage-secret setup --server https://vault.example.com
.Ed
.Ss Check access
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sage-secret check
.Ed
.Ss Run with an environment file
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sage-secret run --env tunnel.env -- sage-tunnel list
.Ed
.Ss Resolve an inline reference
.Bd -literal -offset indent
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=bw:cloudflare-tunnel-startr sage-secret run -- sage-tunnel list
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Errors return 1. On success, commands return 0, except
.Cm run
returns the command's own exit status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bw 1 ,
.Xr security 1 ,
.Xr sage-tunnel 1
